From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sapphire <sapphire@local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0332: gpu: small-only zero default without persistent 1G map

Default gpu_zero to 0 so large render targets (>= 256 KB) are not zeroed
on every GEM_NEW, avoiding per-allocation 0.5 ms WC bzero stalls without
mapping the 1 GiB GPOOL_PA range into compact 4K kernel VA space.
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SapphireGpu.cpp | edit
 1 file changed

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SapphireGpu.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SapphireGpu.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SapphireGpu.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SapphireGpu.cpp
@@ -3762,6 +3762,6 @@
 		static int zero_all = -1;
 		if (zero_all < 0) {
-			int z = 1;              /* 0215: on by default again (gpu_zero=0: 0205's way); see below */
+			int z = 0;              /* 0332: zero small (<256 KB) buffers only by default; gpu_zero=1 zeroes all */
 			PE_parse_boot_argn("gpu_zero", &z, sizeof(z));
 			zero_all = z != 0;
 		}
-- 
